senses.gloss:
Valmīka denotes an ‘ant-hill’ in the later Saṃhitās^1 and the
Brāhmaṇas.^2
1) Taittirīya Saṃhitā, i. 1, 3, 4;
Kāṭhaka Saṃhitā, xix. 2; xxxi. 12;
xxxv. 19; Vājasaneyi Saṃhitā, xxv. 8.
2) Śatapatha Brāhmaṇa, ii. 6, 2, 17;
Bṛhadāraṇyaka Upaniṣad, iv. 4, 10;
Taittirīya Brāhmaṇa, i. 1, 3, 4.
